# Ruleset: HTTP DNS addresses
#
# Expects a reject policy.
#
# The service addresses of the mainland HTTP DNS products, which SDKs dial by address so no name rule sees them: Tencent DNSPod D+, Alibaba Cloud HTTPDNS and Baidu Cloud HTTPDNS. Only addresses the vendors dedicate to the service belong here; an address shared with a CDN would take unrelated traffic with it. 119.29.29.29 and 223.5.5.5 are general public resolvers and stay out.
#
# Reference it in the address block, after every name rule, so a named request that lands on one of these addresses is classified by its name.

IP-CIDR,119.29.29.98/31,no-resolve
IP-CIDR,180.76.76.200/32,no-resolve
IP-CIDR,182.254.116.117/32,no-resolve
IP-CIDR,182.254.118.119/32,no-resolve
IP-CIDR,203.107.1.0/24,no-resolve
